  "lineage": "Neapolitan-language art-popular song tradition, comprising the canonical Naples-and-Campania song-repertoire from the mid-nineteenth-century onward (the genre crystallized around the 1839 Piedigrotta Festival commissioned songs and continuing through the 1890s \"golden age\" with O sole mio, 1898 by Eduardo di Capua and Giovanni Capurro). The form combines elements of Italian operatic-melodic-vocabulary, Mediterranean folk-traditions, and Neapolitan-dialect literary poetry. Distinguished by canzone napoletana's strict use of the Neapolitan language (a distinct Romance language closely related to but distinct from standard Italian).",
